## Visual Entity-Relationship (ER) Diagram

A visual SVG version of this diagram has been generated at [`docs/diagrams/er-diagram-visual.svg`](./diagrams/er-diagram-visual.svg).

```mermaid
erDiagram
    DEPARTMENT ||--o{ USER : "employs (GRO)"
    DEPARTMENT ||--o{ GRIEVANCE : "handles"
    USER ||--o{ GRIEVANCE : "files (as Citizen)"
    GRIEVANCE ||--o{ RESOLUTION_LOG : "tracks"
    USER ||--o{ RESOLUTION_LOG : "writes (as GRO)"
    GRIEVANCE ||--o| FEEDBACK : "receives"

    DEPARTMENT {
        bigint id PK "AUTO_INCREMENT"
        string name "UNIQUE, NOT NULL"
        string code "UNIQUE, NOT NULL"
        string description
        datetime created_at
    }

    USER {
        bigint id PK "AUTO_INCREMENT"
        string name "NOT NULL"
        string email "UNIQUE, NOT NULL"
        string password "NOT NULL"
        string phone_number
        string role "ENUM: CITIZEN, GRO"
        bigint department_id FK "Nullable, GRO only"
        datetime created_at
    }

    GRIEVANCE {
        bigint id PK "AUTO_INCREMENT"
        string tracking_id "UNIQUE, NOT NULL"
        string subject "NOT NULL"
        text description "NOT NULL"
        string status "ENUM: PENDING, IN_PROGRESS, RESOLVED, REJECTED"
        string priority "ENUM: LOW, MEDIUM, HIGH"
        bigint citizen_id FK "References users.id"
        bigint department_id FK "References departments.id"
        datetime created_at "NOT NULL"
    }

    RESOLUTION_LOG {
        bigint id PK "AUTO_INCREMENT"
        bigint grievance_id FK "References grievances.id"
        bigint gro_id FK "References users.id"
        string action_taken "NOT NULL"
        text remarks "NOT NULL"
        datetime logged_at "NOT NULL"
    }

    FEEDBACK {
        bigint id PK "AUTO_INCREMENT"
        bigint grievance_id FK "UNIQUE, References grievances.id"
        int rating "CHECK: 1 to 5"
        text comment
        boolean is_appealed "DEFAULT FALSE"
        datetime submitted_at "NOT NULL"
    }
```

---

## 1. Objective

The objective of this practical work is to design, implement, and test the relational database schema for a **Government Grievance Redressal Portal**. The work covers normalized table creation, primary and foreign key constraint enforcement, sample civic data insertion in referential integrity safe order, multi-table JOIN operations (INNER, LEFT, RIGHT, FULL, and NATURAL JOINs), composite query analysis, and intentional SQL constraint violation testing for practical database debugging.

---

## 2. Database Structure

The database contains **5 core normalized tables**: `departments`, `users`, `grievances`, `resolution_logs`, and `feedbacks`.

The relationships are strictly implemented using primary keys and foreign keys to guarantee municipal audit integrity:
- `departments -> users`: A department employs multiple Grievance Redressal Officers (GROs) ($1:N$).
- `departments -> grievances`: A department is assigned to handle multiple municipal grievances ($1:N$).
- `users -> grievances`: A registered citizen submits and tracks multiple grievance tickets ($1:N$).
- `grievances -> resolution_logs`: A grievance accumulates sequential action logs and remarks during resolution ($1:N$).
- `users (GRO) -> resolution_logs`: A GRO writes resolution log entries across assigned department grievances ($1:N$).
- `grievances -> feedbacks`: A resolved grievance receives exactly one citizen satisfaction feedback and appeal rating ($1:1$).

