### 5.2 LEFT JOIN
**Description:** Returns all rows from the left table (`departments`), plus matched rows from the right table (`grievances`). Where a department has no grievances, columns return as `NULL`.

```sql
SELECT 
    d.name AS department_name,
    d.code,
    g.tracking_id,
    g.subject,
    g.status
FROM departments d
LEFT JOIN grievances g
    ON d.id = g.department_id;
```

#### MySQL CLI Output:
```text
mysql> SELECT 
    ->     d.name AS department_name,
    ->     d.code,
    ->     g.tracking_id,
    ->     g.subject,
    ->     g.status
    -> FROM departments d
    -> LEFT JOIN grievances g
    ->     ON d.id = g.department_id;
