### 5.4 FULL JOIN (Emulated in MySQL via UNION)
**Description:** Returns all rows from both tables, with `NULL` on whichever side lacks a match. Implemented in MySQL using `LEFT JOIN` and `RIGHT JOIN` unified by `UNION`.

```sql
SELECT 
    d.name AS department_name,
    g.tracking_id,
    g.subject,
    g.status
FROM departments d
LEFT JOIN grievances g ON d.id = g.department_id
UNION
SELECT 
    d.name AS department_name,
    g.tracking_id,
    g.subject,
    g.status
FROM departments d
RIGHT JOIN grievances g ON d.id = g.department_id;
```

