### 5.5 NATURAL JOIN
**Description:** Automatically joins two tables on all identically named columns across their schemas. Because `grievances` and `resolution_logs` each have their own independent primary key `id`, MySQL attempts to match `grievances.id = resolution_logs.id`. When these IDs represent distinct entities or do not align, an empty set is produced, demonstrating why explicit `ON` predicates are required in robust database development.

```sql
SELECT 
    id,
    subject,
    action_taken
FROM grievances
NATURAL JOIN resolution_logs;
```

#### MySQL CLI Output:
```text
mysql> SELECT 
    ->     id,
    ->     subject,
    ->     action_taken
    -> FROM grievances
    -> NATURAL JOIN resolution_logs;
Empty set (0.00 sec)
```

---

### 5.6 MULTI-TABLE COMPOSITE JOIN (Civic Audit Pipeline)
**Description:** Joins `users` (Citizen), `grievances`, `departments`, `resolution_logs`, and `users` (GRO) across four relational foreign keys to reconstruct the complete resolution history.

```sql
SELECT 
    g.tracking_id,
    c.name AS citizen,
    d.code AS dept,
    gro.name AS officer,
    rl.action_taken,
    rl.logged_at
FROM grievances g
INNER JOIN users c ON g.citizen_id = c.id
INNER JOIN departments d ON g.department_id = d.id
INNER JOIN resolution_logs rl ON rl.grievance_id = g.id
INNER JOIN users gro ON rl.gro_id = gro.id
ORDER BY rl.logged_at DESC;
```

#### MySQL CLI Output:
```text
mysql> SELECT 
    ->     g.tracking_id,
    ->     c.name AS citizen,
    ->     d.code AS dept,
    ->     gro.name AS officer,
    ->     rl.action_taken,
    ->     rl.logged_at
    -> FROM grievances g
    -> INNER JOIN users c ON g.citizen_id = c.id
    -> INNER JOIN departments d ON g.department_id = d.id
    -> INNER JOIN resolution_logs rl ON rl.grievance_id = g.id
    -> INNER JOIN users gro ON rl.gro_id = gro.id
    -> ORDER BY rl.logged_at DESC;
+---------------+--------------+------+--------------------+-----------------------------+---------------------+
| tracking_id   | citizen      | dept | officer            | action_taken                | logged_at           |
