## 6. Intentional SQL Error Testing & Constraint Debugging

### 6.1 Foreign Key Constraint Violation (Error 1452)
Attempting to insert a grievance for a non-existent citizen (`citizen_id = 9999`):

```text
mysql> INSERT INTO grievances (tracking_id, subject, description, status, priority, citizen_id, department_id, created_at)
    -> VALUES ('GRV-TEST-FAIL', 'Illegal Waste Dumping', 'Waste dumped near lake', 'PENDING', 'HIGH', 9999, 1, NOW());
ERROR 1452 (23000): Cannot add or update a child row: a foreign key constraint fails (`grievance_db`.`grievances`, CONSTRAINT `fk_grievance_citizen` FOREIGN KEY (`citizen_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`))
```

### 6.2 Duplicate Key Entry Violation (Error 1062)
Attempting to insert a duplicate unique department code (`code = 'WSB'`):

```text
mysql> INSERT INTO departments (name, code, description, created_at)
    -> VALUES ('Water Services Agency', 'WSB', 'Duplicate department code test', NOW());
ERROR 1062 (23000): Duplicate entry 'WSB' for key 'departments.code'
```

### 6.3 Check Constraint Violation (Error 3819)
Attempting to submit citizen feedback with a rating outside the permitted $1–5$ range (`rating = 7`):

```text
mysql> INSERT INTO feedbacks (grievance_id, rating, comment, is_appealed, submitted_at)
    -> VALUES (1, 7, 'Invalid rating score test', 0, NOW());
ERROR 3819 (HY000): Check constraint 'chk_feedback_rating' is violated.
```
